    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (81.17) and **Trea Turner** (79.76) leading the charge as our clear-cut offensive anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Yesavage, carrying an elite 0.448 xwOBA that maximizes his output in a favorable hitting environment. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** is a must-start not only for his 79.76 score but because of the specific tactical advantage he holds today: Palmquist\u2019s slow delivery against a soft-tossing lefty creates a prime environment for **Trea Turner** to exploit the base paths, reinforcing our organizational strategy of prioritizing elite speed in 5x5 Roto. **Christian Yelich** (74.32) also provides excellent leverage, as his matchup against Lowder allows him to capitalize on a significant SP skill gap that boosts his efficiency well into our \"Strong\" category.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with several players facing tougher arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (42.58) and **Carson Benge** (44.34) both teeter on the edge of our efficiency floor due to unfavorable lefty-lefty matchups against Manaea and Imanaga, respectively. The most difficult decision on the bench today was **Nelson Velazquez** (41.88); he pushed hard for a spot based on his elite 0.421 xwOBA, but the optimizer ultimately sidelined him in favor of the higher-floor options because he faces the difficult Bratt, whose 3.00 xERA drags down the overall scoring projection. **Junior Caminero** (60.47) and **Caleb Durbin** (69.13) remain our most reliable mid-tier plays, with **Caleb Durbin** benefiting from a similar speed-friendly matchup against the deliberate delivery of Freeland. We are monitoring the status of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Pedro Ramirez** closely, though both remain benched today as they fell well short of our 40.0 efficiency threshold given their poor historical BvP and SP matchups.",
